From 62ab133c55d204a67c21e1519a85f4edc0ec8cc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 11:24:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sunxi: add H616 audio hub driver

The audio hub of the H616 is a crossbar switch between three APBIF DMA
interfaces, two digital audio mixers and four I2S/PCM controllers. Only
three of the I2S controllers reach pins, the second one is wired to the
HDMI controller.

Register the four I2S controllers as DAIs of one component, each with a
fixed APBIF interface, and move the samples with the dmaengine PCM
helpers. As every DAI needs its own DMA channel, the channels are
requested up front and the PCM operations are open coded instead of
using the generic dmaengine PCM, which keeps only one channel pair per
component.

Playback towards HDMI accepts IEC958 subframes on top of ordinary PCM.
Those carry the payload and the PCUV bits in different places than the
HDMI controller expects, so they are rewritten in place once the
application has handed them over, and are spread over up to four
transmit lines, so that eight channel and high bit rate streams work as
well. Asking for an explicit appl_ptr sync keeps that translation on the
mmap path as well, where there is no copy to hook into.

The mixers, the freely programmable routing and the fourth I2S
controller are not modelled yet.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/sunxi/Kconfig            |   18 +-
 sound/soc/sunxi/Makefile           |    1 +
 sound/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h616-ahub.c | 1299 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 1315 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 sound/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h616-ahub.c

